<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;Hmmm. Thanks. Maybe it's not the character I think it is:

&lt;c&gt;
&gt; $ perl -wMstrict -lE "qq/Screenshot-2024-02-23-at-1.05.14&amp;#8239;AM.png/ =~ /\s/ and say 'OK' or die" 
Died at -e line 1.
&lt;/c&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The #8239 popped in after submitting this post. It's not actually in the code. 

&lt;p&gt;#8239 is 202F in hex. I don't get this. 

&lt;p&gt;This doesn't even work:

&lt;c&gt;
&gt; $ perl -wMstrict -lE "qq/Screenshot-2024-02-23-at-1.05.14&amp;#8239;AM.png/ =~ /\x{202F}/ and say 'OK' or die"                                                                                                                                                                                                            
Died at -e line 1.
&lt;/c&gt;

